    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        30,
        1200
      ],
      "size": [
        1000,
        280
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 7,
      "mode": 0,
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Custom rig workflow (experimental):\n1. In Load 3D (Advanced), select a rigged FBX, GLB or glTF with one skeleton/root.\n2. CLIP Loader: google-t5/t5-base model.safetensors renamed t5-base.safetensors; type stable_audio.\n3. Install Blender 4.2+; the node detects it automatically. No path setup is needed.\n4. Set forward_axis to the facing direction seen in Load 3D (Y-up coordinates).\n5. Select your video, DINOv2-Large and MoCapAnything checkpoint.\nThe prepared reference feeds Capture; the SAME prepared rig feeds Animate Rig.\nThe viewers show the skeleton and skinned mesh. Use Play in their animation controls.\nReference features come from one rest pose: motion quality and scale can differ from upstream dataset preparation.\nConnect reference_image to Preview Image to inspect preparation. Connect model_3d to native Save 3D to export GLB."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
